<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n17469" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fā^brē-făcĭo</span></b> ,
			fēci, factum, 3, v. a., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to make</i>, <i>frame</i>, <i>fashion</i>, or <i>do skilfully</i> (very rare; perh. to be written
			separately fabre facio). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">classem fabrefecit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Aur.
						Vict. Vir. Ill. 38, 1</span></i>
			 (dub., al. fabricavit): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fabrefieri ex auro,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Exod. 31, 4</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">levioribus et ad id fabrefactis navigiis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					37, 27, 5</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">argenti aerisque fabrefacti vis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					26, 21, 8</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">id. 34, 52, 5</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Amm. 29, 1</span></i>.—*
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fallaciam,</span>”
				<i>to forge</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut.
					Cas. 5, 1, 8</span></i>
			; cf.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fecit fabre,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Stich. 4, 1, 64</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
